q.en:
Spot the mistake in this GB function:
def size_gb(n, b):
    return round(n * b / 1e6, 2)

q.ta:
இந்த GB function-இல் உள்ள பிழையைக் கண்டறியுங்கள்:
def size_gb(n, b):
    return round(n * b / 1e6, 2)

uth_example:
gpu_gb = 80
model_params = {"Llama-70B": 70e9, "MoE-400B": 400e9}
bytes_per = {"fp32": 4, "bf16": 2, "int8": 1, "int4": 0.5}

table = {}
for model, params in model_params.items():
    table[model] = {}
    for fmt, b in bytes_per.items():
        gb = round(params * b / 1e9, 1)
        table[model][fmt] = (gb, -(-gb // gpu_gb))      # GPUs needed (ceil)

for model, row in table.items():
    print(model)
    for fmt, (gb, gpus) in row.items():
        print(f"  {fmt:5} {gb:7} GB -> {int(gpus)} x 80GB GPU")
